The IDE now shows a member's proof-dependency warnings once when a refining module checks again the override of a class member it inherits (https://github.com/erniecohen/dafny/issues/424). Since https://github.com/erniecohen/dafny/issues/404, that check belongs to a copy of the member, at the member's own position. The warnings that are computed once an implementation has verified, such as those of `--warn-redundant-assumptions` and `--warn-contradictory-assumptions`, were kept per position and not per member. So the base member and its copy each carried over all of them at every resolution, and the IDE showed the base member's warnings twice after the first edit, four times after the second, and so on until the next verification. They are now kept per member, like the verification tasks at that position, and each verification replaces only its own member's warnings.
